From 0e99f0168c704c6c0b8ce5d6b4611c88075c43cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 22:33:57 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 31/43] Exit status 0 when the player or the game ends the run

main returned 4 whenever the runtime had a stop reason, and every stop has
one: closing the window, Quit in the menu, the input script's quit and the
game's own sceKernelExitGame all exited with 4, the code of an error stop. The
reasons for those endings are now named constants in system.hpp, and
is_requested_stop() tells them from the others. They exit with 0; any other
stop (no runnable thread, an unmapped address, a missing import) still exits
with 4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 host/hle/hle_media.cpp  |  9 +++++----
 host/hle/hle_system.cpp |  3 ++-
 host/main.cpp           |  4 +++-
 host/system.hpp         | 13 +++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 23 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

